From 3c76f4c882f545ed84fc747b6c4613afc67dd794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:23:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WireGuard server: dual-family peers, port clashes refused, a
 failed start logged (102.8 line)

- A new peer gets the next free host number in both families, and an IPv6 default route only when
  it has an IPv6 address. Existing peers are not rewritten.
- Saving a port that another VPN server of the router uses (OpenVPN, WireGuard, IPsec) is refused
  when either side changed in that save.
- rc logs a WireGuard server whose interface could not be brought up.
- The page's OpenVPN status poll joined its four values with a plain ';', which httpd reads as the
  end of a parameter, so only the first was read. They are joined with %3B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/wireguard.c           |  16 ++-
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_VPNServer.asp | 127 ++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 126 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/wireguard.c b/release/src/router/rc/wireguard.c
index 4ee0e8fcb1..1994ce5509 100644
